==Finnish==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|fi|urj-fin-pro|*üdin||bone marrow}} (compare {{cog|et|üdi}}, {{cog|krl|yjin}}), from {{inh|fi|fiu-pro|*wideme||bone marrow}} (compare {{cog|se|ađa||(bone with) marrow}}, {{cog|myv|удем||marrow; intellect}}, {{cog|mhr|вем||marrow}}, {{cog|hu|velő||marrow}}).

===Pronunciation===
{{fi-pronunciation|yDin}}

===Noun===
{{head|fi|noun}}

# [[core]], [[kernel]], [[nucleus]], the central part of something
#: {{syn|fi|sydän|yty|sisus}}
#: {{coi|fi|'''ydin'''perhe|'''nuclear''' family}}
# {{lb|fi|figuratively}} [[core]], [[point]], essential content, essence; often with the genitive of {{m|fi|asia||matter, topic}}
#: {{syn|fi|juuri}}
#: {{ux|fi|päästä asian '''ytimeen'''|to [[get to the point|get '''to the point''']]|inline=1}}
# {{lb|fi|anatomy}} the most [[central]], [[inner]] part of certain body parts
#: {{coi|fi|[[luuydin|luu'''ydin''']]|bone '''marrow'''}}
#: {{coi|fi|[[selkäydin|selkä'''ydin''']]|spinal '''cord'''}}
## {{lb|fi|anatomy}} [[quick]] {{gloss|sensitive tissue inside a nail}}
# {{lb|fi|botany}} [[pith]] {{gloss|soft spongy substance in the center of the stems of many plants and trees}}
# {{lb|fi|geology}} [[core]] {{gloss|center or inner part of a planet}}
#: {{ux|fi|Maapallon '''ydin''' jaetaan sisä'''ytimeen''' ja ulko'''ytimeen'''.|The Earth's '''core''' is divided into the inner '''core''' and the outer '''core'''.|inline=1}}
# {{lb|fi|physics}} [[nucleus]] {{gloss|massive, positively charged core of an atom}}
#: {{coi|fi|'''ydin'''fysiikka|'''nuclear''' physics}}
#: {{ux|fi|Atomi'''ydin''' on atomin keskellä sijaitseva protoneista ja yleensä myös neutroneista koostuva muodostuma.|The '''nucleus''' is the region consisting of protons and usually neutrons at the center of an atom.|inline=1}}
# {{lb|fi|computing}} [[core]] {{gloss|individual computer processor}}
#: {{ux|fi|Tämä ohjelma käyttää kaikkia '''ytimiä'''.|This application uses all the '''cores'''.|inline=1}}
# {{lb|fi|mathematics}} [[kernel]] {{gloss|set of elements mapped to zero; set of members of a fuzzy set that are fully included}}
# {{lb|fi|computing}} [[kernel]] {{gloss|central part of many computer operating systems}}
#: {{ux|fi|Linux viittaa Linux-'''ydintä''' käyttävien Unixin kaltaisten käyttöjärjestelmien perheeseen.|Linux refers to the Linux '''kernel''' used by the Unix-like family of operating systems.|inline=1}}
# {{lb|fi|linguistic}} [[nucleus]] {{gloss|centre of a syllable}}

